last month Activision announced that the  ps3 and xbox 360 versions of call of  duty black ops 3 would not be including  the game single-player campaign now  while a lot of SBS games are popular for  their multiplayer here are six which  have really awesome single-player  campaign  Call of Duty is both defined what the  shooter genre is today and defined the  controversy over annual installments  that said no installment is nailed at  single-player campaign quite as well as  call of duty 4 modern warfare  modern warfare was the first game in the  franchise to depart from the world war 2  setting as the name implies you could  now get your hands on modern weaponry  technology and vehicles in addition to  the series of signature shootouts Modern  Warfare's campaign included clever and  stressful stealth missions as well as  intense narrative scenarios like the  gut-wrenching experience of your player  character slowly dying after the  explosion of a nuclear bomb the tight  pacing and blockbuster success of Modern  Warfare set a standard that plenty of  other games of shamelessly imitated ever  since before we got our hands on it it  would have been hard to guess that  Wolfenstein the new order would have a  great campaign given that Wolfenstein 3d  was pretty bare-bones as far as story  goes but it did and it was great in the  game's ultimate history version of world  war ii the third reich has completely  taken over Europe after the protagonist  BJ blaskowitz has fallen into a coma he  gets out of it and naturally it's up to  him to shoot everything back to justice  the brash gunplay and limited health  regeneration gave the action a great  sense of urgency and the writing takes  its cheesiness in its stride is  surprisingly funny and explores  interesting themes related to the nature  of war and to the impact on those caught  up in it as far as I'm concerned little  girl ghosts will always be terrifying  clearly monolith productions thought  much the same thing when they created  first encounter assault recon or if you  prefer beer it may have a very silly  acronym for a name but fear has a truly  creepy atmosphere and a detailed horror  story to scare the crap out of you even  though you're playing a badass soldier  with lots of guns uncovering what's  causing those supernatural bumps in the  night in fear is exceptionally cool and  the campaign cleverly balances its jump  scares and sure  with narrative twists and turns you know  it has really great stories books Metro  2033 was based on a book and it has a  great single-player campaign  you play as Artyom in a post nuclear  apocalyptic Russia where everything has  gone to [ __ ]  Society has retreated underground and  are now living in the labyrinth Ian's  metro system metro 2033 succeeds in its  pacing and rich game world one moment  you're shooting frantically at  horrifying mutants lurking in the dark  and the next you're speaking with  survivors and finding out how life goes  on even after the worst happened it also  replicates that post-apocalyptic  survival tension by having your bullets  be your currency do you shoot your way  through a problem or sneak past it to  save for upgrades your first glimpse of  rapture from the relative security of a  bathysphere is one of the coolest  moments in gaming and bioshock's  campaign just keeps delivering after  that Bioshock is one of my favorite  games of all time and the story is  wonderful  you play as Jack who finds himself  uncovering the messy social and  political history of the formerly  utopian city of Rapture and dealing with  the result of its downfall jack has a  hell of a time dealing with the mutated  former citizens of rapture getting  injected with plasmids being  double-crossed dealing with batshit  crazy larger-than-life characters and  dealing with the consequences of his  choices I'm sure many of you would agree  that this list of excellent singleplayer  FPS campaigns would not be complete  without half-life 2 you probably don't  need me to reiterate what half-life is  done for the FPS genre and gaming in  general but I'll do my best to summarize  carp life two largely defined what it  was to integrate a nuanced  compelling narrative into shooter  exploring and interacting with the world  as a means of storytelling proves to be  a very effective way of drawing you into  the story as its unravels great gunplay  and puzzles aside half life to succeeds  by building a fascinating world filled  with characters you care about and an  exciting sci-fi plot to get swept up in  let me know down in that comment section  which singleplayer FPS campaign is your  favorite and be sure let me know if I  missed out on mentioning your pick I  will catch you again next week
 

